# Initial Setup's CAN GPS Order page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigGPSOrder.cs
# (PLAN.md §13.6 row 70).
#
# The claim: Activate disables the page for good on a vehicle without GPS1_CAN_OVRIDE, else reads
# the detected node ids (GPS_CAN_NODEID1, GPS_CAN_NODEID2) and the overrides (GPS1_CAN_OVRIDE,
# GPS2_CAN_OVRIDE) and lists each override that is set and each detected node that is neither
# (ConfigGPSOrder.cs:21-51) in the Designer's grid - Order, Name, NodeID, GPS1, GPS2 - whose two
# button columns set an override to the row's node id and run Activate again (:62-86).
#
# SITL's copter is firmware 4.5+: it lists GPS1_CAN_OVRIDE, so the page is enabled, but names the
# detected id GPS1_CAN_NODEID, so Activate's read of GPS_CAN_NODEID1 is the C#'s
# NullReferenceException - logged by BackstageView.ActivatePage, the grid left empty, as it is in
# Mission Planner on this firmware. Which read threw is a fact. Nothing is written.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-gpsorder.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.GPS1_CAN_OVRIDE 0

click tab-setup
expect config.gpsorder.active false
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigGPSOrder
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigGPSOrder
expect config.gpsorder.active true
expect config.gpsorder.enabled true
expect config.gpsorder.heading UAVCAN GPS Order
expect config.gpsorder.note Set the GPS order if required
expect config.gpsorder.columns Order,Name,NodeID,GPS1,GPS2
expect config.gpsorder.rows 0
expect config.gpsorder.threw NullReferenceException at GPS_CAN_NODEID1
expect config.gpsorder.write none
expect config.gpsorder.message none

# Choosing another page hides this one; it is IActivate only.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
settle 1
expect config.gpsorder.active false
